<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōmŭlus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the founder and first king of Rome</i>,
				<i>worshipped after his death as</i> Quirinus,
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
				4</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 12, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ep. 108, 31</span></i>. — Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōmŭlĕus</span></b>  (Romuleus,
			Auct. Perv. Ven. 72), a, um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Romulus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				<i>Rome</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 5, 260</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">casa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. Fragm. 21, 6</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 654</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2,
			1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fera,</span>”
				<i>the she-wolf</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 104</span></i>
			 et saep.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōmŭlus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Romulus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ficus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 412</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hasta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 4, 26: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tellus,</span>”
				<i>Roman</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 877</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 5, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				C. S. 47</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 793</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōmŭlāris</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of Romulus</i>:
			ficus; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">v. Ruminalis: populus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 13</span></i>
			
			<i>in carm.</i> 2 <i>fin.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rōmŭlĭdae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the posterity of Romulus</i>, <i>the Romans</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Lucr.
				4, 683</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 638</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 1,
			31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 1,
		6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
